<title>ITALY: Italy March producer prices rise 0.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy March producer prices rise 0.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics office ISTAT gave the following Italian producer price data for March.</p>
<p>    PRODUCER PRICES	   March 97   Feb 97	 March 96</p>
<p>    Year/year change	  +0.9 pct    +0.8 pct     +3.7 pct</p>
<p>    Month/month change	+0.3 pct    +0.0 pct     +0.2 pct</p>
<p>    Index (base 1995=100)    102.9	 102.6	  102.0</p>
<p>Istat gave the following general breakdown:</p>
<p>				   Mo/Mo change (%)    Yr/Yr change (%)</p>
<p>    Consumer goods		  +0.5		    +0.7</p>
<p>    Investment goods		+0.4		    +1.8</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods	    +0.1		    +0.8</p>
<p>It gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown:</p>
<p>    Sector			    mo/mo (%)	     yr/yr (%)</p>
<p>    Energy products		 +0.9		    +6.7</p>
<p>    Minerals			   0.0		    +8.8</p>
<p>    Non-metal minerals	    +0.6		    +2.1</p>
<p>    Chemicals			 -0.1		    +0.5</p>
<p>    Metal works		     +0.4		    -1.5</p>
<p>    Cars and parts		  +0.5		    +2.3</p>
<p>    Food, drink and tobacco     +0.9		    -0.3</p>
<p>    Clothing and textiles	 +0.1		    +0.2</p>
<p>    Leather goods		    0.0		    +2.2</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
